{{- /*
  Which of the three machines this is, as one word: macos, omarchy or xrdp.

  .chezmoi.os stopped being enough once a second Linux machine arrived. It used
  to mean "the RDP work VM", so i3, xterm and a 12pt kitty all keyed on it — and
  an Omarchy desktop is Linux too, running Hyprland on Wayland, where every one
  of those is wrong.

  Detected rather than asked, and included rather than stored in the generated
  chezmoi.toml. A prompt would need every machine to re-run `chezmoi init`
  before the key existed, and a template reading a missing key fails the apply.
  Computing it on each use needs nothing on any machine. Omarchy is the
  directory its package installs everything into; any other Linux is taken to
  be the RDP machine, which is what `linux` meant before this file existed.

  Use: {{ $desktop := includeTemplate "desktop" . }}
*/ -}}
{{- if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" -}}
macos
{{- else if stat "/usr/share/omarchy" -}}
omarchy
{{- else -}}
xrdp
{{- end -}}
